:true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> The order of the equation is 2.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> The order of the equation is not defined.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> The degree of the equation is 2.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, b)<br />\nThe degree of the differential equation is the power of the highest order derivative whereas the order of the differential equation is the order of the highest order derivative present in the equation. Thus, given differential equation has the order 2. Since, the given differential equation cannot be written as a polynomial in all the differential coefficients, the degree of the equation is not defined.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":25,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A fair die is rolled. Let R denote the event of obtaining a number less than or equal to 5 and S denote the event of obtaining an odd number. Then <img src=\"/media/68347a1e0fde7e78c231b0b5ec4537289e9454ce.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.6","high":"0.6"},"solution":"<p>0.60 (0.50 - 0.70)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/72cd1a0d66dd83720ff511d202c2938b32f80376.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":26,"type":"MSQ","correct":"C,D","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The value of ‘<em>b</em>’ for which <em>u</em>(<em>x</em>, <em>y</em>) = <em>e<sup>bx</sup></em> cos5y is harmonic is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> +3</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> -3</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> +5</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> -5</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c, d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/b67ee7ebe47ae667ea7b6ad466c90e9970dd3470.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":27,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the differential equation 4y′′(x) + 64y(x) = 0 with initial conditions y(0) = 0 and y′(0) = 1024.<br />\nThe value of y at x = 1 is _____ (upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"-193.74","high":"-193.74"},"solution":"<p>-193.74 (-195.00 - - 192.00)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/c70db9267e8a4a9ef6fbdc1dd685dd71cfb38f72.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":28,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A box contains 2 washers, 3 nuts and 4 bolts. Items are drawn from the box at random one at a time without replacement. The probability of drawing 2 washers first followed by 3 nuts and subsequently the 4 bolts is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/68cd947cb43706dedfc9a3c50030da0e153e3612.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/64dc9ccb5bd2681c9ae2a926fc2aa65eec7f779d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/50661619928678c69dc3e36ff8c2b684c49dc41f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/40cc10c93929f18a81f517c034813bd5401ea755.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/483810b3f7c430e1b39ded6520050d5b677ddf3e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/968d59288843cb8af96ed5349db3ce48d4ddaa4a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":29,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Let <em>k</em> be a positive real number and let</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/0a5f3405f20d5ec0d0b117fe641e7b50468cf86e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>If det (Adj A) + det (adj B) = 106, then k is equal to _____.</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4.5","high":"4.5"},"solution":"<p>4.5</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/ef1427ba2117d02d95e220abce6293443fa57463.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":30,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Let R be a region in the first quadrant of xy plane enclosed by the two curves as shown below.<br />\nWhich of the following expression does represent the area of the region <em>R</em>?</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/32bba8c5d6f621ebc63ee30e871686f867fa2bb8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/d9c7bf763978d5c6a009cb12f10a64c93150f80e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/431af3acc0a7d109a90eb31bd4094a206788d27a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/79a6bb51c6f92452f98b9403e4fd51e1afcd2aeb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/4cf4b3af085f1c23e36254a9776cf322dee3d242.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b, c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/24f95f29f5a01653c8c661abc29975fa937479da.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":31,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The value of <img src=\"/media/a45f8342fb4f6f530c0ad34ea3561bcd460e5c6e.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/f7e397b1867dc36d4f5c2db134df7e3abb9a5493.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/b1704a558d5f9c899d16a40b502af44895d38642.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/cdca69e1714855e8d89345856d274470f51a5333.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/0934d55fe47dc575dab44f86d6284d1ab04bac6f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/1f56e4100cb5fda6bd71b2944f225e173f6950f9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":32,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Let <em>f</em>(<em>x</em>) = 3x<sup>3</sup> – 7x<sup>2</sup> + 5x + 7. The absolute minimum value of f(x) over the interval [0, 2] is ____.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"7","high":"7"},"solution":"<p>7 (7 - 7)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/93b542eab98a6f4f16e5ab65215b23cfe2016b71.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":33,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The Newton-Raphson method is used to solve the equation <em>x</em><sup>3</sup> – 5<em>x</em><sup>2</sup> + 6<em>x</em> + <em>k</em> = 0. Taking the initial guess as <em>x</em> = 5, the solution obtained at the end of first iteration is 4, then the value of <em>k</em> is __________.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1","high":"1"},"solution":"<p>1 (1 - 1)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/4204f7d3214b3a49bdcba9918ce08d978edbd91b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"}],"questionCount":33,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:19.426Z"}